diff --git a/cpp/tests/CONTROL_PLANE_FAIRNESS.md b/cpp/tests/CONTROL_PLANE_FAIRNESS.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..39022ba
--- /dev/null
+++ b/cpp/tests/CONTROL_PLANE_FAIRNESS.md
@@ -0,0 +1,167 @@
+# UCXX progress-thread control-plane fairness
+
+This branch tests and fixes starvation of delayed control-plane callbacks when
+`ucp_worker_progress()` remains continuously busy with data-plane completions.
+The observed production symptom is three consecutive 3-second
+`ucp_ep_create()` callback timeouts while established endpoints continue
+transferring data.
+
+The fix limits each dedicated progress-thread drain to 256 UCP progress calls.
+It then returns to the outer worker loop, where delayed request submissions and
+generic pre/post callbacks are serviced. Public `Worker::progress()` retains its
+existing drain-until-idle behavior.
+
+The remaining starvation path was an entire delayed-request snapshot ahead of
+endpoint creation. Endpoint creation now uses a separate control-pre queue.
+Delayed requests are submitted in chunks of 64, with control-pre serviced
+between chunks. Generic-pre remains behind the complete original request
+snapshot, preserving its request-submission barrier semantics.
+
+## Build
+
+Create the normal UCXX development environment, then:
+
+```bash
+./build.sh clean libucxx libucxx_tests -n
+```
+
+The test executable is:
+
+```text
+cpp/build/gtests/UCXX_TEST
+```
+
+The commands below are also wrapped by:
+
+```bash
+cpp/tests/run_control_plane_fairness.sh fast
+cpp/tests/run_control_plane_fairness.sh backlog-repro
+cpp/tests/run_control_plane_fairness.sh endpoint-repro
+cpp/tests/run_control_plane_fairness.sh natural-backlog
+cpp/tests/run_control_plane_fairness.sh stress
+```
+
+## Fast regression gate
+
+```bash
+timeout 60s cpp/build/gtests/UCXX_TEST \
+  --gtest_filter='ProgressDrainTest.*:WorkerProgressThreadTest.GenericPreRunsWhileProgressRemainsContinuouslyBusy'
+```
+
+The generic-pre test is deterministic. It models a worker that never reports
+idle and fails on the unbounded implementation without requiring RDMA hardware.
+The delayed-submission characterization also records how many request callbacks
+are processed before a generic-pre callback. On the current implementation that
+is the entire request snapshot.
+
+## Delayed-request backlog reproduction
+
+The production run still timed out after the UCP progress drain was bounded.
+The next scheduling stage before endpoint creation is the delayed-request queue:
+
+```text
+delayed requests -> generic pre (ucp_ep_create) -> UCP progress -> generic post
+```
+
+Two disabled regression tests isolate that path. They are disabled so a normal
+UCXX test run remains usable while the bug is intentionally present.
+
+First, reproduce a shortened generic-pre deadline:
+
+```bash
+cpp/tests/run_control_plane_fairness.sh backlog-repro
+```
+
+This queues 128 delayed-request callbacks whose aggregate runtime exceeds a
+100 ms control-pre deadline. The test-only parent commit processes the entire
+request snapshot first and fails with:
+
+```text
+control-pre callback timed out behind the delayed-request snapshot
+```
+
+With the priority control queue, the callback executes before the first request
+chunk and the test passes. A separate deterministic test confirms generic-pre
+still observes the complete original request snapshot.
+
+Second, exercise the real endpoint creation path:
+
+```bash
+cpp/tests/run_control_plane_fairness.sh endpoint-repro
+```
+
+This creates a worker with delayed submission enabled, parks its progress
+thread inside the first callback of a four-second delayed-request snapshot, and
+then requests a real loopback endpoint. The test-only parent commit emits the
+same three-second `ucp_ep_create` retry warning seen in production and fails its
+two-second endpoint-latency requirement. The priority control queue should
+create the endpoint after the current 64-request chunk instead of the complete
+snapshot.
+
+The reproducers report the configured backlog, observed control-plane latency,
+and the number of delayed requests processed ahead of the control operation as
+GoogleTest properties. A scheduling fix should make both disabled tests pass
+without reducing or removing the backlog. Their settings can be overridden:
+
+```text
+UCXX_TEST_BACKLOG_REQUEST_COUNT
+UCXX_TEST_BACKLOG_CALLBACK_DELAY_US
+UCXX_TEST_BACKLOG_CONTROL_DEADLINE_MS
+UCXX_TEST_ENDPOINT_BACKLOG_REQUEST_COUNT
+UCXX_TEST_ENDPOINT_BACKLOG_CALLBACK_DELAY_US
+UCXX_TEST_ENDPOINT_BACKLOG_MAX_LATENCY_MS
+```
+
+Finally, measure the same path without artificial callback delays:
+
+```bash
+cpp/tests/run_control_plane_fairness.sh natural-backlog
+```
+
+This sweeps 8,192, 32,768, and 131,072 pairs of real delayed `tagRecv` and
+`tagSend` requests queued before a late endpoint. It validates every transfer
+and reports endpoint latency for each backlog size. Override the sweep with a
+space-separated list:
+
+```bash
+UCXX_TEST_NATURAL_BACKLOG_COUNTS='32768 65536 131072 262144' \
+  cpp/tests/run_control_plane_fairness.sh natural-backlog
+```
+
+If latency scales toward three seconds, aggregate request submission is enough
+to explain the production timeout. If it remains low even at large backlogs,
+the next target is a slow request callback or lock encountered by the progress
+thread rather than queue length alone.
+
+## Real UCXX delayed-submission stress
+
+```bash
+timeout 120s env \
+  UCXX_TEST_FAIRNESS_BATCH_SIZE=32768 \
+  UCXX_TEST_FAIRNESS_ENDPOINT_COUNT=256 \
+  UCXX_TEST_FAIRNESS_MAX_ENDPOINT_LATENCY_MS=2000 \
+  cpp/build/gtests/UCXX_TEST \
+    --gtest_filter='WorkerProgressThreadTest.LateEndpointsCompleteDuringDelayedTagTraffic' \
+    --gtest_repeat=10 \
+    --gtest_break_on_failure
+```
+
+The test:
+
+1. starts a polling progress thread with delayed request submission enabled;
+2. keeps a rolling window of tag requests outstanding on an established
+   endpoint, replenishing each completed slot;
+3. creates new endpoints after traffic is active;
+4. requires every endpoint creation to finish below the configured deadline;
+5. transfers data over every late endpoint; and
+6. verifies each request callback fires exactly once.
+
+The three environment variables are deliberately tunable. Start with the
+values above. `UCXX_TEST_FAIRNESS_BATCH_SIZE` is the number of traffic slots
+kept outstanding; increase it if the host drains the background work too
+quickly to reproduce the old failure. The test reports
+`background_transfers_completed`, `late_endpoints_created`, and
+`max_endpoint_latency_ms` as GoogleTest properties.
+
+These tests create only process-local UCX workers and endpoints. They do not
+modify NIC, firmware, routing, IBM Storage Scale, or Slurm state.
